var documenterSearchIndex = {"docs":
[{"category":"section","location":"#BiorthoDMRG.jl","page":"Home","text":"","title":"BiorthoDMRG.jl"},{"category":"module","location":"#BiorthoDMRG.BiorthoDMRG","page":"Home","text":"BiorthoDMRG\n\nTwo-site biorthogonal DMRG for non-Hermitian MPOs.  With |ψ⟩ = P{ℓψ}|φψ⟩ and |χ⟩ = P{ℓχ}|φχ⟩ in the biorthonormal gauge P{ℓχ}†P{ℓψ} = 1, each bond update of biorthodmrg solves\n\nP_{ℓχ}† H P_{ℓψ} |φ_ψ⟩ = E |φ_ψ⟩,     P_{ℓψ}† H† P_{ℓχ} |φ_χ⟩ = Ē |φ_χ⟩,\n\nnormalizes ⟨φχ|φψ⟩ = 1, and refactorizes both blocks, in one shared orthonormal basis or in a biorthonormal pair of bases.\n\nFor the steady state of a Lindbladian 𝓛, steadystate holds the left state fixed at the vectorized identity |1⟩, which the doubled site indices determine, and keeps |ρ⟩ = P{ℓρ}|φρ⟩ in the mixed canonical gauge. With the test map P{ℓ1} of LindbladProjMPO, which satisfies P{ℓ1}†P{ℓρ} = 1 and P{ℓ1}|φ1⟩ = |1⟩ for |φ1⟩ = P_{ℓρ}†|1⟩, each bond update solves\n\nP_{ℓ1}† 𝓛 P_{ℓρ} |δφ⟩ = P_{ℓ1}† 𝓛 P_{ℓρ} |φ_ρ⟩,     ⟨φ_1|δφ⟩ = 0,\n\nand replaces |φρ⟩ by |φρ⟩ - |δφ⟩.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BiorthoDMRG.BiorthoDMRG"},{"category":"type","location":"#BiorthoDMRG.AbstractBiorthoProjMPO","page":"Home","text":"AbstractBiorthoProjMPO\n\nSupertype for operators projected onto the open window of a biorthogonal pair (chi, psi). Subtypes implement ITensorMPS.position!(P, chi, psi, ℓ) to move the window to sites ℓ:ℓ+1, ITensors.product(P, v) to apply the projected operator to v, and adjoint_product(P, v) to apply its adjoint. P(v) is the same as product(P, v).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BiorthoDMRG.AbstractBiorthoProjMPO"},{"category":"type","location":"#BiorthoDMRG.BiorthoObserver","page":"Home","text":"BiorthoObserver(; H=nothing, residual_tol=0.0)\n\nObserver for biorthodmrg and steadystate that records one entry per sweep. energies holds the energy, conditions the condition number ‖chi‖‖psi‖/|⟨chi|psi⟩|, and stats the SweepStats. steadystate records the vectorized identity as chi and rho as psi.\n\nIf H is given, residuals holds the relative residuals of psi and chi, computed with H and its adjoint Hdag, and the run stops after the first sweep in which both are below residual_tol. Without H, the run never stops early.\n\nResiduals are used instead of energy changes because the energy need not converge monotonically. They resolve values only down to about √eps, so residual_tol must be larger than that.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BiorthoDMRG.BiorthoObserver"},{"category":"type","location":"#BiorthoDMRG.BiorthoProjMPO","page":"Home","text":"BiorthoProjMPO(H::MPO)\n\nH projected onto the open window, with chi as the bra and psi as the ket. H is the full MPO; env caches the left and right environments of ⟨chi|H|psi⟩ outside the window. BiorthoProjMPO(H) creates an empty cache, and the first position! fills it.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BiorthoDMRG.BiorthoProjMPO"},{"category":"type","location":"#BiorthoDMRG.BiorthoProjMPS","page":"Home","text":"BiorthoProjMPS(Lref::MPS, Rref::MPS)\n\nThe rank-one operator |Rref⟩⟨Lref| projected onto the open window, with chi as the bra and psi as the ket. It is the deflation term for a converged pair (Lref, Rref); BiorthoProjMPO_MPS applies the weight.\n\nLref and Rref are the reference states. cacheL caches the environments of ⟨Lref|psi⟩ and cacheR those of ⟨Rref|chi⟩. braL is ⟨Lref| restricted to the window through psi's environments, and braR is ⟨Rref| restricted through chi's; position! recomputes both.\n\nBiorthoProjMPS(Lref, Rref) rescales Rref so that ⟨Lref|Rref⟩ = 1, gives both references new link indices so they cannot collide with those of chi or psi, and creates empty caches.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BiorthoDMRG.BiorthoProjMPS"},{"category":"type","location":"#BiorthoDMRG.BiorthoProjSum","page":"Home","text":"BiorthoProjSum(terms, coeffs)\n\nΣₐ coeffs[a] * terms[a], a linear combination of projected operators on the same window. The adjoint conjugates the coefficients.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BiorthoDMRG.BiorthoProjSum"},{"category":"type","location":"#BiorthoDMRG.EnvCache","page":"Home","text":"EnvCache(N)\n\nLeft and right environments of an N-site chain around an open window.\n\nLR[k] holds the left environment of sites 1:k for k ≤ lpos and the right environment of sites k:N for k ≥ rpos; sites lpos+1:rpos-1 form the window. Each environment contracts the ket, the operator, and the conjugated bra over its sites. The operator is an MPO, or the identity when it is nothing.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BiorthoDMRG.EnvCache"},{"category":"type","location":"#BiorthoDMRG.LindbladProjMPO","page":"Home","text":"LindbladProjMPO(𝓛::MPO)\n\nThe Lindbladian 𝓛, an MPO on doubled sites ordered as by doubled_siteinds, projected onto a window of rho for the steady-state problem. The window covers two physical sites, the four doubled sites ℓ:ℓ+3 with ℓ odd, or the whole chain when it has one physical site, so both of its cuts lie between physical sites. The left state is held fixed at the vectorized identity |1⟩, which the site indices of 𝓛 determine; it is stored in id as an MPS of deltas and is never updated or truncated. rho is in the mixed canonical gauge, so its blocks L_ρ and R_ρ outside the window are isometries.\n\nAcross a cut between physical sites |1⟩ = |1_L⟩ ⊗ |1_ℓ⟩ ⊗ |1_R⟩ factorizes, and the bra side is the test map P_{ℓ1} = L₁ ⊗ 1 ⊗ R₁ with\n\nL₁ = L_ρ + (1 - L_ρ L_ρ†) |1_L⟩⟨1_L|L_ρ / ⟨1_L|L_ρ L_ρ†|1_L⟩\n\nand R₁ its mirror image. Then L₁† L_ρ = 1 and L₁ L_ρ† |1_L⟩ = |1_L⟩, so P_{ℓ1}† P_{ℓρ} = 1 and P_{ℓ1} |φ₁⟩ = |1⟩ with |φ₁⟩ = P_{ℓρ}† |1⟩. Since ⟨1|𝓛 = 0, ⟨φ₁| is an exact left null vector of the projected operator P_{ℓ1}† 𝓛 P_{ℓρ}, and ⟨φ₁|phi⟩ = ⟨1|rho⟩ for the window tensor phi of rho. The denominator is ‖⟨1_L|L_ρ‖², nonzero whenever ⟨1|rho⟩ ≠ 0.\n\nenv, idenv and trenv cache the environments of ⟨rho|𝓛|rho⟩, ⟨1|𝓛|rho⟩ and ⟨1|rho⟩, from which position! assembles envL = L₁†(·)L_ρ and envR = R₁†(·)R_ρ. bra1 is ⟨φ₁|, and cosine is ‖φ₁‖/‖1‖ = 1/‖P_{ℓ1}‖, the cosine between |1⟩ and the range of P_{ℓρ}. id has its own link indices, so they cannot collide with those of rho.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BiorthoDMRG.LindbladProjMPO"},{"category":"type","location":"#BiorthoDMRG.MPIBiorthoSum","page":"Home","text":"MPIBiorthoSum(term, comm; mode, checksync = false)\n\nProjected operator whose terms are spread over the ranks of comm. Each rank holds one part of the Hamiltonian, for example term = BiorthoProjMPO(H_p) with H = Σ_p H_p, and builds the environments for that part only. Every rank must call the constructor.\n\nWith mode = :root, only rank 0 runs biorthodmrg, and the other ranks run serve!. Rank 0 sends the other ranks every updated site tensor and every window vector, and collects the sum of their products. Every decision of the eigensolver and the truncation is therefore made on rank 0 alone, and the mode does not depend on reproducible arithmetic. Rank 0 calls stopservice! when it is done, for example in a finally block, which releases the other ranks.\n\nWith mode = :replicated, every rank runs biorthodmrg on the same inputs. The sum of the products is returned to every rank, and each rank repeats the eigensolver and the truncation on identical data. The ranks stay in step only if their arithmetic is bitwise reproducible, which in practice means the same CPU type and a fixed number of BLAS threads. With checksync = true, each position! compares the newly replaced site tensors across ranks and throws if they differ. Wrap the observer in MPIObserver and set outputlevel = 0 on every rank except 0.\n\nThe terms may have Float64 entries on some ranks and ComplexF64 entries on others. Each product is promoted to the common entry type before the sum is taken.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BiorthoDMRG.MPIBiorthoSum"},{"category":"type","location":"#BiorthoDMRG.MPIObserver","page":"Home","text":"MPIObserver(obs, comm)\n\nWrap obs for mode = :replicated. obs runs on rank 0 of comm only (pass nothing elsewhere), and its stopping decision is broadcast so that every rank leaves the sweep loop together.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BiorthoDMRG.MPIObserver"},{"category":"type","location":"#BiorthoDMRG.SiteTracker","page":"Home","text":"SiteTracker()\n\nReferences to the site tensors of chi and psi at the last call of changedsites!.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BiorthoDMRG.SiteTracker"},{"category":"type","location":"#BiorthoDMRG.SweepStats","page":"Home","text":"SweepStats\n\nWorst-case diagnostics over the bonds of one sweep.\n\nmaxtruncerr is the largest truncation error of either state, sigma_min the smallest cosine between the kept left and right bases, cosangle_min the smallest cosine between the local left and right eigenvectors before normalization, and maxresidual the largest relative residual of a local left or right eigenvector. For steadystate, sigma_min is the smallest cosine between the vectorized identity and the kept space of rho, and cosangle_min the smallest cosine between the local steady state and the trace functional. SweepStats() is the starting value before any bond is visited.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BiorthoDMRG.SweepStats"},{"category":"method","location":"#BiorthoDMRG.BiorthoProjMPO_MPS-Tuple{ITensorMPS.MPO, Vector{<:Tuple{ITensorMPS.MPS, ITensorMPS.MPS}}}","page":"Home","text":"BiorthoProjMPO_MPS(H::MPO, refs::Vector{Tuple{MPS,MPS}}; weight)\n\nH plus deflation terms for converged eigenpairs: the BiorthoProjSum of BiorthoProjMPO(H) with coefficient 1 and one BiorthoProjMPS(L_i, R_i) per pair with coefficient weight. Each pair is (L_i, R_i) = (chi_i, psi_i), in the order biorthodmrg returns them. For exact pairs with nondegenerate E_i, each E_i moves to E_i + weight and every other eigenpair is unchanged, so choose weight to move the converged eigenvalues out of the region selected by which.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BiorthoDMRG.BiorthoProjMPO_MPS"},{"category":"method","location":"#BiorthoDMRG._biortho_basis-Tuple{ITensors.ITensor, ITensors.ITensor, Any}","page":"Home","text":"_biortho_basis(phi_psi, phi_chi, is; biortho_cutoff, tags, svd_kwargs...)\n\nBiorthonormal bases for phi_psi and phi_chi on the indices is.\n\nEach block is truncated by an SVD with svd_kwargs. The two kept bases are then rotated and rescaled, using the SVD of their overlap, so that Xchi† Xpsi is the identity on the new link index, which carries tags. \n\nThe singular values of the overlap are the cosines of the angles between the  kept subspaces; those at or below biortho_cutoff are dropped.  Also returns both truncation spectra and sigma_min, the smallest kept cosine.  Dense indices only.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BiorthoDMRG._biortho_basis"},{"category":"method","location":"#BiorthoDMRG.adjoint_mpo-Tuple{ITensorMPS.MPO}","page":"Home","text":"adjoint_mpo(H::MPO)\n\nH† as an MPO: conjugate every tensor and exchange the prime levels of its site indices (tagged \"Site\").  dag(H) alone is the elementwise conjugate, not H†.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BiorthoDMRG.adjoint_mpo"},{"category":"function","location":"#BiorthoDMRG.adjoint_product","page":"Home","text":"adjoint_product(P::AbstractBiorthoProjMPO, v::ITensor)\n\nApply the adjoint of the projected operator P to v, using the same environments as product.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BiorthoDMRG.adjoint_product"},{"category":"method","location":"#BiorthoDMRG.biorthodmrg-Tuple{AbstractBiorthoProjMPO, ITensorMPS.MPS, ITensorMPS.MPS, ITensorMPS.Sweeps}","page":"Home","text":"biorthodmrg(H::MPO, psi0::MPS; nsweeps, maxdim, mindim, cutoff, kwargs...)\nbiorthodmrg(H::MPO, chi0::MPS, psi0::MPS; ...)\nbiorthodmrg(H::MPO, refs::Vector{Tuple{MPS,MPS}}, chi0::MPS, psi0::MPS; weight, ...)\nbiorthodmrg(PH::AbstractBiorthoProjMPO, chi0::MPS, psi0::MPS, sweeps::Sweeps; ...)\n\nTwo-site DMRG for the left and right eigenvectors of a non-Hermitian H. Returns (E, chi, psi): psi is the right eigenvector and chi the left eigenvector, normalized so that ⟨chi|psi⟩ = 1, and E = ⟨chi|H|psi⟩, all up to truncation.\n\nWith one initial state, chi0 = psi0. With refs, previously converged pairs (chi_i, psi_i) are deflated by shifting their eigenvalues by weight. The last form takes any projected operator and a Sweeps object; the others build both.\n\nEach bond update calls biorthoproblemsolver. which selects the eigenvalue as in KrylovKit.eigsolve, and target and howmany choose among Ritz pairs. basis chooses :shared (stable, larger bond dimension) or :biorthonormal (compact, unbounded local spectrum); see biorthoreplacebond!. biortho_cutoff drops cosines between the kept left and right bases at or below it, and applies only to :biorthonormal. observer is an ITensorMPS observer or a BiorthoObserver. outputlevel and the eigsolve_* keywords are as in ITensorMPS.dmrg. noise must be zero and indices must be dense.\n\nFor the steady state of a Lindbladian, whose eigenvalue and left eigenvector are known, use steadystate.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BiorthoDMRG.biorthodmrg"},{"category":"method","location":"#BiorthoDMRG.biorthogonalize!-Tuple{ITensorMPS.MPS, ITensorMPS.MPS, Int64}","page":"Home","text":"biorthogonalize!(chi, psi, j; normalize=true, kwargs...)\n\nBring chi and psi into biorthonormal form centered on site j, in place, and return them.\n\nEach bond is refactorized with biorthoreplacebond!, sweeping in from both ends toward j. Afterwards both states share every link index, sites left of j are left-biorthonormal, and sites right of j are right-biorthonormal. Left-biorthonormal means that contracting dag(chi[k]) with psi[k] over their left link and site index gives the identity; right-biorthonormal is the mirror of this.\n\nWith normalize=true, chi[j] is rescaled so that ⟨chi|psi⟩ = 1. kwargs are passed to biorthoreplacebond!. Without truncation, the states are unchanged when, at every bond, the kept bases of chi and psi have the same dimension and no overlap cosine is dropped. Otherwise they are truncated.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BiorthoDMRG.biorthogonalize!"},{"category":"method","location":"#BiorthoDMRG.biorthoproblemsolver-Tuple{AbstractBiorthoProjMPO, ITensors.ITensor, ITensors.ITensor}","page":"Home","text":"biorthoproblemsolver(P, phi_psi, phi_chi; which=:SR, target=:which, howmany, tol, krylovdim, maxiter, verbosity)\n\nSolve the local eigenproblem of the projected operator P from both sides. Arnoldi on P, starting from phi_psi, gives E and the right eigenvector; Arnoldi on the adjoint, starting from phi_chi and targeted at conj(E), gives the left eigenvector.\n\ntarget=:which takes the first right pair in KrylovKit's which order. target=:overlap takes the right pair, among howmany, that overlaps most with the current left block. tol, krylovdim, maxiter and verbosity are passed to KrylovKit.eigsolve.\n\nReturns (E, phi_psi, phi_chi, info), normalized so that ⟨phi_chi|phi_psi⟩ = 1 with equal norms. info.cosangle is the cosine of the angle between the two vectors before normalization, which vanishes at an exceptional point of P. info.residual is the larger of the relative residuals of the two vectors.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BiorthoDMRG.biorthoproblemsolver"},{"category":"method","location":"#BiorthoDMRG.biorthoreplacebond!-Tuple{ITensorMPS.MPS, ITensorMPS.MPS, Int64, ITensors.ITensor, ITensors.ITensor}","page":"Home","text":"biorthoreplacebond!(chi, psi, ℓ, phi_chi, phi_psi; ortho, basis=:biorthonormal, biortho_cutoff=0, svd_kwargs...)\n\nSplit the two-site blocks phi_chi and phi_psi back into sites ℓ and ℓ+1 of chi and psi, truncating with svd_kwargs. With ortho=\"left\", site ℓ receives the new bases and site ℓ+1 the remainders, so the window moves right; ortho=\"right\" does the reverse. Both states get the same new link index.\n\nbasis=:shared gives both states one orthonormal basis that captures both blocks. The local operator is then an orthogonal compression of H, whose eigenvalues stay within the numerical range of H. basis=:biorthonormal gives each state its own basis, which is more compact, but the local operator then has eigenvalues that can lie far outside the spectrum of H.\n\nReturns the spectra of both blocks and sigma_min, which is 1 for :shared. For :biorthonormal, if no cosine is dropped and both blocks keep the same dimension, the relative error of each block is at most (1 + 1/sigma_min) * sqrt(truncerr).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BiorthoDMRG.biorthoreplacebond!"},{"category":"method","location":"#BiorthoDMRG.condition_number-Tuple{ITensorMPS.MPS, ITensorMPS.MPS}","page":"Home","text":"condition_number(chi, psi)\n\nκ = ‖χ‖‖ψ‖ / |⟨χ|ψ⟩| ≥ 1; it equals 1 iff |χ⟩ ∝ |ψ⟩.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BiorthoDMRG.condition_number"},{"category":"method","location":"#BiorthoDMRG.doubled_siteinds-Tuple{Vector{<:ITensors.Index}}","page":"Home","text":"doubled_siteinds(s)\n\nSite indices for vectorized density matrices on the sites s, ordered [s₁, b₁, s₂, b₂, …]. The physical index sⱼ carries the row (ket) index of ρ, and bⱼ, a new index of the same site type tagged \"bra\", carries the column (bra) index.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BiorthoDMRG.doubled_siteinds"},{"category":"method","location":"#BiorthoDMRG.reposition!-Tuple{BiorthoDMRG.EnvCache, Any, ITensorMPS.MPS, ITensorMPS.MPS, Int64}","page":"Home","text":"reposition!(E, op, bra, ket, ℓ; nsite=2)\n\nMove the window to sites ℓ:ℓ+nsite-1. \n\nCached environments are reused and only missing ones are computed, so bra and ket must be unchanged at every site covered by a reused environment.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BiorthoDMRG.reposition!"},{"category":"method","location":"#BiorthoDMRG.residuals-Tuple{ITensorMPS.MPO, ITensorMPS.MPS, ITensorMPS.MPS, Number}","page":"Home","text":"residuals(H, chi, psi, E; Hdag=adjoint_mpo(H)) -> (r_psi, r_chi)\n\nRelative residuals ‖H|ψ⟩ − E|ψ⟩‖/‖ψ‖ and ‖H†|χ⟩ − Ē|χ⟩‖/‖χ‖, from ‖A|x⟩ − λ|x⟩‖² = ⟨Ax|Ax⟩ − 2Re(λ̄⟨x|A|x⟩) + |λ|²⟨x|x⟩.  The expansion cancels large terms, so the resolution is limited to about √eps relative to ‖A‖.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BiorthoDMRG.residuals"},{"category":"function","location":"#BiorthoDMRG.serve!","page":"Home","text":"serve!(P::MPIBiorthoSum)\n\nWorker loop for mode = :root, run on every rank of P.comm except 0: apply this rank's term on request from rank 0 until rank 0 calls stopservice!(P). An error on a worker aborts the communicator, since rank 0 would otherwise wait in the reduction.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BiorthoDMRG.serve!"},{"category":"method","location":"#BiorthoDMRG.sssolver-Tuple{LindbladProjMPO, ITensors.ITensor}","page":"Home","text":"sssolver(P::LindbladProjMPO, phi; tol, krylovdim, maxiter, verbosity)\n\nLocal solver of steadystate. With ⟨φ₁| = P.bra1 the trace functional on the window, phi is rescaled to unit trace, ⟨φ₁|phi⟩ = 1, and GMRES started from zero solves\n\nP δ = P phi,    ⟨φ₁|δ⟩ = 0.\n\nThen x = phi - δ is the right null vector of P with unit trace, the result of one step of inverse iteration with the shift at the known eigenvalue 0. ⟨φ₁| is an exact left null vector of P, so P maps the orthogonal complement of |φ₁⟩ into itself, and the projections onto that complement remove only rounding errors. The solution is unique if and only if the null space of P is one-dimensional and not orthogonal to |φ₁⟩. tol, krylovdim, maxiter and verbosity are passed to KrylovKit.linsolve.\n\nReturns (λ, x, info). λ is the Rayleigh quotient of x, zero at convergence. info.cosangle is the cosine between x and |φ₁⟩, which vanishes as the null vector of P becomes orthogonal to |φ₁⟩, and info.residual is ‖P x‖ / ‖x‖.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BiorthoDMRG.sssolver"},{"category":"method","location":"#BiorthoDMRG.steadystate-Tuple{ITensorMPS.MPO, ITensorMPS.MPS, ITensorMPS.Sweeps}","page":"Home","text":"steadystate(𝓛::MPO; nsweeps, maxdim, mindim, cutoff, kwargs...)\nsteadystate(𝓛::MPO, rho0::MPS; ...)\nsteadystate(𝓛::MPO, rho0::MPS, sweeps::Sweeps; ...)\n\nDMRG for the steady state of the Lindbladian 𝓛, an MPO on doubled sites ordered as by doubled_siteinds. Returns (λ, rho): rho is the right null vector of 𝓛 with unit trace, and λ its Rayleigh quotient, which vanishes at convergence, both up to truncation.\n\nThe left state stays fixed at the vectorized identity, which LindbladProjMPO builds from the site indices of 𝓛, and only rho is swept, in the mixed canonical gauge. Each window covers two physical sites, so both of its cuts lie between physical sites, where the identity factorizes and the test map of LindbladProjMPO exists whenever tr ρ ≠ 0. At each window sssolver removes the traceless part of the window tensor, which is then split back into site tensors by SVDs truncated with maxdim, mindim and cutoff. rho0 is any state on the sites of 𝓛 with nonzero trace; without it, the sweeps start from the maximally mixed state. The last form takes a Sweeps object; the others build it from the keywords.\n\nobserver is an ITensorMPS observer or a BiorthoObserver, which records the vectorized identity as the left state. outputlevel is as in ITensorMPS.dmrg, and the linsolve_* keywords are passed to sssolver. noise must be zero and indices must be dense.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BiorthoDMRG.steadystate"},{"category":"function","location":"#BiorthoDMRG.stopservice!","page":"Home","text":"stopservice!(P::MPIBiorthoSum)\n\nEnd serve! on every worker. Rank 0 calls it once biorthodmrg has returned or thrown, for example in a finally block.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BiorthoDMRG.stopservice!"},{"category":"method","location":"#BiorthoDMRG.vectorized_identity-Tuple{Vector{<:ITensors.Index}}","page":"Home","text":"vectorized_identity(d)\n\nThe identity matrix as an MPS on the doubled sites d, ordered as by doubled_siteinds, with bond dimension dim(sⱼ) inside each pair and 1 between pairs. Its overlap with a vectorized density matrix is the trace, so inner(vectorized_identity(d), rho) is tr ρ.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BiorthoDMRG.vectorized_identity"},{"category":"module","location":"#BiorthoDMRG.Models","page":"Home","text":"Models\n\nModel Hamiltonians as MPOs, for examples and tests. All chains are open.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BiorthoDMRG.Models"},{"category":"method","location":"#BiorthoDMRG.Models.ising_imaginary_field-Tuple{Any}","page":"Home","text":"ising_imaginary_field(sites; J = 1.0, hx, hz)\n\nTransverse-field Ising chain with an imaginary longitudinal field. Each bond carries -J Z_j Z_{j+1} and each site -hx X_j - i hz Z_j, with Pauli X, Z. The matrix is complex symmetric, so each left eigenvector is the complex conjugate of the corresponding right eigenvector. At hz = 0 it is Hermitian. Use \"S=1/2\" sites.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BiorthoDMRG.Models.ising_imaginary_field"},{"category":"method","location":"#BiorthoDMRG.Models.lindbladian-Tuple{ITensorMPS.MPO, Vector{ITensors.ITensor}, Vector{<:ITensors.Index}}","page":"Home","text":"lindbladian(H::MPO, jumps::Vector{ITensor}, d; cutoff = 1e-14)\n\nThe Lindbladian ρ ↦ -i[H, ρ] + Σₖ (Lₖ ρ Lₖ† - ½{Lₖ†Lₖ, ρ}) as an MPO acting on vectorized density matrices on the doubled sites d = doubled_siteinds(s). H is an MPO on the physical sites s, and each jump operator is an ITensor on a single physical site, for example sqrt(γ) * op(\"S-\", s[1]). The terms are summed and compressed with cutoff.\n\nThe steady state is the right null vector with unit trace, and vectorized_identity(d) is an exact left null vector, so tr(Oρ) is inner(vectorized_identity(d), apply(O, rho)). steadystate(𝓛; nsweeps) finds the steady state with the left state held fixed at the identity.\n\nA single-site \"C\" carries no Jordan–Wigner string, so fermionic jump operators should  be written in a spin representation.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BiorthoDMRG.Models.lindbladian"},{"category":"method","location":"#BiorthoDMRG.Models.nonreciprocal_ssh-Tuple{Any}","page":"Home","text":"nonreciprocal_ssh(sites; t1, t2, γ, V = 0.0)\n\nSSH chain of spinless fermions with non-reciprocal intracell hopping, sites ordered A₁, B₁, A₂, B₂, …. Cell j carries (t1 + γ/2) c†_{A_j} c_{B_j} + (t1 - γ/2) c†_{B_j} c_{A_j}, neighboring cells are joined by t2 (c†_{B_j} c_{A_{j+1}} + h.c.), and V adds V n_x n_{x+1} on every bond. For |t1| > |γ|/2 it is similar to the Hermitian chain with intracell hopping sign(t1) * sqrt(t1^2 - γ^2/4), so the spectra agree. Use \"Fermion\" sites; the number of sites must be even.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BiorthoDMRG.Models.nonreciprocal_ssh"},{"category":"method","location":"#BiorthoDMRG.Models.xxz-Tuple{Any}","page":"Home","text":"xxz(sites; Δ, g = 0.0, J = 1.0, h = 0.0)\n\nXXZ chain with non-reciprocal spin flips. Each bond carries J/2 (e^g S⁺_{j+1} S⁻_j + e^-g S⁻_{j+1} S⁺_j) + Δ Sᶻ_j Sᶻ_{j+1} and each site -h Sᶻ_j. For any g it equals S H₀ S⁻¹ with H₀ the Hermitian chain at g = 0 and S = exp(g Σ_j j Sᶻ_j), so the spectra agree, and the right and left eigenvectors are S|ψ₀⟩ and S⁻¹|ψ₀⟩. Under Jordan–Wigner it is the interacting Hatano–Nelson model. Use \"S=1/2\" sites.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BiorthoDMRG.Models.xxz"}]
}
